{% doc %}
  Self-hosted font faces.

  THEME STORE BLOCKER. The requirements say fonts must come from the
  `font_picker` setting, whose library is Shopify's and cannot be extended by a
  theme; a bundled font file fails review. This exists because Forum is not in
  that library and the brand calls for it.

  Removing it before submission is a clean delete, by design:
    1. this file
    2. the `{% render 'custom-fonts' %}` capture in snippets/css-variables.liquid
       and the `case custom` branches around it
    3. the four `font_*_custom` settings in config/settings_schema.json
    4. the font files in assets/
  The named fallback to switch to is in DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md, Phase 11.

  Forum ships one weight and no italic, so bold and italic are synthesized by
  the browser. That is a second reason this cannot go to review as it stands.

  `assets/forum-regular.woff2` is the latin subset from Google Fonts, 24 KB.

  Forum: Copyright (c) 2011 Denis Masharov, Reserved Font Name "Forum",
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Bundling is permitted as long
  as the license travels with the font — the full text is in `licenses/` at the
  repository root, since Shopify's assets directory does not accept .txt.

  @param {string} used - Pipe-separated list of custom font keys in use, so a
    face is only downloaded when a role actually asks for it.

  @example
  {% capture faces %}{% render 'custom-fonts', used: custom_fonts_used %}{% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- if used contains 'forum' -%}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Forum';
  src: url({{ 'forum-regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
{%- endif -%}
